# Phase 5 — Live classes, scheduling, chat & attendance

## Routes
- `POST /api/live/sessions` — instructor/admin schedules a session for an owned course.
- `GET /api/live/sessions` — instructor sessions, student-enrolled course sessions, or admin sessions.
- `PATCH /api/live/sessions/:id` — edit session metadata/status or cancel (owner/admin only).
- `POST /api/live/sessions/:id/join` — creates a short-lived, room-scoped LiveKit token after enrollment/ownership checks.
- `POST /api/live/sessions/:id/attendance/heartbeat` — authenticated attendance heartbeat.
- `POST /api/live/sessions/:id/attendance/leave` — marks student left.
- `GET /api/live/sessions/:id/attendance` — instructor attendance roster.

## Environment
Set `LIVEKIT_URL`, `LIVEKIT_API_KEY`, and `LIVEKIT_API_SECRET` in server env. LiveKit chat is provided by the LiveKit `VideoConference` UI.

## Attendance behavior
Students are added when they request a session join. The client sends a heartbeat every 30 seconds while connected. Attendance seconds accumulate by elapsed time between pulses, capped at 45 seconds per pulse. Browser closure/network failure can delay leave marking; treat heartbeat-based attendance as approximate.

## Test checklist
1. Instructor schedules session for own course; scheduling another instructor's course returns 403.
2. Student with enrollment sees the session; a non-enrolled student cannot join.
3. Room is unavailable before its 15-minute join window.
4. Instructor and eligible student receive LiveKit token scoped to that session's private room.
5. Verify in-room video/audio and built-in chat with two test accounts.
6. Student heartbeat increments attendance, leave sets state to left, reconnect increments join count.
7. Instructor sees only owned session attendance; another instructor receives 403.
8. Cancelled/completed sessions cannot be joined.

## Operational notes
- Configure LiveKit networking, TLS, quotas, and credentials. Never expose API secret in frontend.
- Session lifecycle changes are API-driven; production may add LiveKit webhooks for authoritative room participant events.
- Attendance indicates connected presence only, not focus or participation.
- For scale, consider a unique index migration and retention/export policy for attendance records.
